WEBVTT

00:11:29.875 --> 00:11:31.143
at the same time,

00:11:31.167 --> 00:11:34.101
or possibly even ahead of the time
that people are infectious.

00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:36.143
But certainly, let's say at the same time,

00:11:36.167 --> 00:11:38.226
regardless of whether they're symptomatic.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.351
And so you could --

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:43.143
Those people would
immediately go back home

00:11:43.167 --> 00:11:45.268
and the rest of the population
should be OK,

00:11:45.292 --> 00:11:46.976
we should be able to get work done,

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.518
in that thought experiment, right?

00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:52.393
DA: Right, in that thought
experiment, exactly, yeah.

00:11:52.417 --> 00:11:53.684
CA: But the trouble is,

00:11:53.708 --> 00:11:58.143
that that would mean doing,
whatever, like, 200 million tests a day.

00:11:58.167 --> 00:11:59.976
DA: Right, exactly.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.184
CA: Which is many, many orders
of magnitude more than we have